<main>
  <h1>Hardware</h1>
  <p class="lede">What this deployment of local_LLM is actually running on — generated by <code>scripts/detect-hardware.sh</code>, not hand-written. Re-run it after any hardware change to keep this page accurate.</p>

  <table>
    <tr><td>GPU</td><td>GPU_NAME_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>VRAM (total / free)</td><td>GPU_VRAM_TOTAL_PLACEHOLDER / GPU_VRAM_FREE_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>GPU driver</td><td>GPU_DRIVER_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>nvidia-container-toolkit</td><td>NVIDIA_TOOLKIT_STATUS_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU</td><td>CPU_MODEL_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU cores (logical)</td><td>CPU_CORES_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>CPU topology</td><td>CPU_TOPOLOGY_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>RAM (total)</td><td>RAM_TOTAL_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Last scanned</td><td>SCAN_DATE_PLACEHOLDER</td></tr>
  </table>

  <p>See <a href="https://github.com/JEA666/local_LLM/blob/main/prompt.md"><code>prompt.md</code></a> for how these numbers turn into a model choice and tuned <code>.env</code>.</p>
</main>

</body>
